<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!-- Android probe mod (Unity 6000.0.61f1, Il2CppInterop 1.5.1, LemonLoader MelonLoader net6).
       The game interop and loader runtime assemblies are referenced from external directories
       supplied on the command line; nothing is downloaded, installed, deployed or copied into
       the output (Private=false). Missing directories or missing UnityEngine.UI.dll /
       UnityEngine.UIModule.dll (the Issue #119 native hit surface) fail with a clear MSBuild
       error.

         dotnet build -c Release ^
           -p:GameInteropDir=<dir with Assembly-CSharp.dll and the UnityEngine.* / Il2Cpp*.dll interop assemblies> ^
           -p:LoaderRuntimeDir=<dir with MelonLoader.dll, 0Harmony.dll, Il2CppInterop.Runtime.dll> ^
           -p:SupportModuleDir=<dir with the loader's SupportModules\Il2Cpp.dll (MonoEnumeratorWrapper)>

       The unmodified desktop sources il2cpp/BoatCapacityProfile.cs,
       il2cpp/PatchPlayer_HoldPurchase.cs,
       il2cpp/PatchWorld_EnemyManager.cs, il2cpp/PatchWorld_FarmCats.cs, il2cpp/FarmCatMovement.cs,
       il2cpp/GreekScaleScope.cs, il2cpp/PatchWorld_Construction.cs, il2cpp/MapWidthPlanner.cs
       and the shared UI files il2cpp/ModPanelStyles.cs, il2cpp/ModPanelControls.cs and
       il2cpp/ImGuiCompat.cs are linked read-only (Compile Include below); il2cpp/MapWidthTerrain.cs,
       il2cpp/PatchWorld_Level.cs and il2cpp/PatchWorld_FastForestRecede.cs are linked with an
       #if ANDROID alias header only, and il2cpp/PatchWorld_DeerPopulation.cs carries the same
       alias header plus the ANDROID-specific opt-in gate, default-off fast exit and captured
       eligibility scope evidence; il2cpp/PatchWorld_OptionalVegetation.cs carries the alias
       header plus the ANDROID FX-seam cut, the default-off debt-free entry gate and the three
       real config writers each saving once on a real change (all shared PC logic and
       preprocessed output are unchanged);
       bare game type names are mapped by GlobalAliases.cs;
       Harmony auto-patch-all is suppressed by AssemblyInfo.cs for explicit Operator
       registration. -->

